rossj@northshore.ecosoft.com (Ross A. Jacobs) writes:

>Hi.  


>1) Heard about a "secret room" at bottom of GMines.  How do you get there?

	There is a secret door, just search.	

>2) What can you do with a unicorn horn?

	(a)pplying a unicorn horn can fix a lot of your ailments.  
Dipping it in some nasty potions turns them to water.

>3) "The Quest":  got there, killed a bunch of Ogres, and Pelias told me
>that I wasn't experienced enough (lev 13).  What am I questing for (I'm
>a neutral barbarian)?

	Firstly, you need to be forteenth level.  Each class quest turns 
up a different artifact and the Bell of Opening which you'll need t get 
the amulet.

>4) How do you get more holy water?

	Drop potions of water on a co-aligned alter and pray.  Make sure 
you god is happy with you first.

>5) I've got Cleaver, Dragonbane, and a +5 rusty dwarvish mattock.  The
>mattock seems to work best.  Do I just need to enchant Dragonbane before
>I notice it works better than the rusty ol' pick?

	I'd say Cleaver is the best of the three.  Dragonbane is only 
useful against Dragons (as the name implies) and the bonuses on the 
mattock don't match the innate bonuses of Cleaver.

>6) Can/should you eat black pudding corpses? What should you do beforehand
>to save yourself from killer heartburn?

	Definetely eat them.  Its a great way to get intrinsics.  Don't 
worry about the heartburn, it's inconsequensial (sp?)

>7) Found a portal to Ludios, but it just drops me into a room out of which
>I can't tunnel or teleport.  I'm not messing with it yet, but what should I
>do when I get there?

	Again, search for the secret door.

>8) What else can you do with altars besides dropping and offering?

	For one, get holy water.  They can be used to change alignments, 
and offering will eventually get you an artifact.

	Hope that helps.


